---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="TD Bank Digital Issuance — Rob Pitt"
  description="Led three teams through a $75M redesign of TD Bank's North American credit program. Research led to a PayPal partnership."
>
  <article class="case-study">
    <header class="case-study__header">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="case-study__meta">TD Bank · 2019–2022 · Remote</p>
        <h1 class="case-study__title">Instant card use, across two countries and three business units.</h1>
        <p class="case-study__lede">
          How might new or existing customers start using their new card immediately? That was the question. Answering it meant leading three cross-functional teams through a $75M redesign, navigating US/Canada regulatory differences, and coming out the other side with a unified experience — plus a PayPal partnership.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="case-study__section case-study__section--wide">
      <figure class="figure figure--split">
        <div>
          <img src="/case-studies/digital-wallet/research/currentprocess.png" alt="High level current process" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Current-state process map.</figcaption>
        </div>
        <div>
          <img src="/case-studies/digital-wallet/research/hmw.png" alt="How might we — convergence" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>How-might-we synthesis.</figcaption>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="figure figure--split">
        <div>
          <img src="/case-studies/digital-wallet/research/diverge.png" alt="Ideation and vote" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Idea divergence and dot-voting.</figcaption>
        </div>
        <div>
          <img src="/case-studies/digital-wallet/research/userflow.png" alt="Two-concept user flow" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Two-concept user flow.</figcaption>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="case-study__section">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <p class="case-study__label">My role</p>
        <p>
          Head of design across three concurrent initiatives. I led a distributed team of designers, researchers, and writers through a full human-centered process: research, ideation, prototyping, usability testing, and delivery. Miro became the enterprise workshop standard on my watch — part of a year-long remote-first adoption effort.
        </p>

        <p class="case-study__label">Process</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Member research to uncover real payment preferences</li>
          <li>Facilitated ideation workshops on digital wallet solutions</li>
          <li>Created and refined multiple concepts around education, security, and convenience</li>
          <li>Validated designs through usability testing on the two lead concepts</li>
          <li>Synthesized findings into experience principles that guided delivery</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-study__section case-study__section--wide">
      <figure class="figure figure--split">
        <div>
          <img src="/case-studies/digital-wallet/wires/debit1.png" alt="Debit concept wireframes v1" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Debit concepts, v1.</figcaption>
        </div>
        <div>
          <img src="/case-studies/digital-wallet/wires/debit2.png" alt="Debit concept wireframes v2" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Debit concepts, v2.</figcaption>
        </div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="figure figure--split">
        <div>
          <img src="/case-studies/digital-wallet/wires/newcc1.png" alt="New credit card wireframes v1" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Credit card, v1.</figcaption>
        </div>
        <div>
          <img src="/case-studies/digital-wallet/wires/newcc2.png" alt="New credit card wireframes v2" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Credit card, v2.</figcaption>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="case-study__section">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <p class="case-study__label">Challenges</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Gaining executive buy-in on design direction inside the US</li>
          <li>Re-aligning the experience to meet requirements from Canadian partners</li>
          <li>Navigating feedback and approvals across three separate business units</li>
          <li>Revising approved designs to accommodate international differences</li>
          <li>Mitigating friction between conflicting opinions on UX direction</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="case-study__label">The result</p>
        <p>
          Research validated that members would adopt mobile wallets if the experience delivered simplicity and security. My team shipped a human-centered vision and design direction to make it real. The work led directly to a PayPal digital-wallets partnership.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="case-study__section case-study__section--wide">
      <figure class="figure">
        <img src="/case-studies/digital-wallet/prototype.gif" alt="V1 prototype in motion" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>V1 prototype in motion.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="case-study__section">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <blockquote>
          "I don't know how... but everything you touch just turns to gold!"
          <cite>— E.K., VP of US Design</cite>
        </blockquote>

        <p class="case-study__label">What I actually did</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Led end-to-end design strategy from research to final recommendations</li>
          <li>Collaborated across disciplines to shape a shared UX vision</li>
          <li>Adapted process for remote collaboration during a critical project timeline</li>
          <li>Set guidance for an intuitive digital wallet experience true to member needs</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="case-study__footer">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <a href="/#shipped" class="case-study__back">← back to all work</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  @import "../../styles/case-study.css";
</style>
